{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the gold</b>. The Gaon [Saadia] says that the bedolach is the small round stones that come out of the water, which are fine, and he likened the manna to them. And Scripture, speaking of the manna alone, says that the shoham is a precious white stone, and it is bright, but we do not know."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as the Gaon [Saadia] per standard convention; Ibn Ezra here appears to report Saadia's interpretation of the manna comparison in Numbers 11:7."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:48.037802895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}